{
  "id": "RAW_122c3b32fe",
  "title": "OpenAI 发布 GPT-6 Astra：一款 105 万上下文窗口、需达到「Critical」网络安全阈值的计算机使用模型",
  "url": "https://www.marktechpost.com/2026/09/03/openai-releases-gpt-6-astra-a-1-05m-context-computer-use-model-gated-behind-a-critical-cyber-threshold/",
  "date": "2026-09-04 05:16:13",
  "author": "Asif Razzaq",
  "siteName": "MarkTechPost",
  "content": "<html>\n <head></head>\n <body>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Today, OpenAI released <a href=\"https://openai.com/index/gpt-6-astra/\">GPT-6 Astra</a>. The company calls it its most intelligent and aligned model, and positions it primarily as a computer-use system rather than a chat model. The pitch is that Astra operates software the way a person does, across browsers, spreadsheets, desktop applications and terminals, and finishes multi-step jobs instead of describing how to do them.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Is it deployable?</strong> Partly, and not on your own hardware. Astra is a closed, hosted model with no released weights, so self-hosting is not an option. It is live today only for organizations in OpenAI’s Trusted Access and <a href=\"https://openai.com/index/expanding-daybreak-as-the-cyber-defense-window-narrows/\">Daybreak</a> programs.</p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-what-is-actually-new\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>What is actually new</strong></h2>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The main change for devs is context handling. Codex previously used compaction, summarizing earlier turns once context filled up. That process discards the detail an agent later needs: why a fix failed, which tests ran, which requirement was added early. Astra instead keeps notes across context windows and searches back into earlier messages and tool output. The feature ships experimental behind a <code>config.toml</code> setting and becomes the Codex default in the coming weeks.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Astra can also ask the user a question while continuing work that does not depend on the answer. That removes a common agent failure where one unresolved decision stalls an entire job.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">On the <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-6-astra\">model page</a>, Astra lists a 1,050,000-token context window, 128,000 max output tokens and an April 30, 2026 knowledge cutoff. Input is text and image, output is text only. <code>reasoning.effort</code> adds two new levels above <code>high</code>: <code>xhigh</code> and <code>max</code>. Tool support covers <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/tools-computer-use\">computer use</a>, hosted shell, apply patch, skills, MCP and tool search. Fine-tuning is not supported.</p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-the-benchmark-picture\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>The benchmark picture</strong></h2>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">OpenAI reports 72.6% on OSWorld V2-Offline against 65.7% for GPT-5.6 Sol, with average task time falling from roughly 75 minutes to 40. Anthropic reports 77.9% for <a href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/claude/fable\">Claude Fable 5.1</a> but says it used a different OSWorld release and should not be compared directly.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Astra scores 98.6% on ARC-AGI-3. That number was produced with a Responses API harness that retains reasoning between turns and uses compaction for long contexts, and OpenAI has <a href=\"https://openai.com/index/how-two-settings-tripled-our-arc-agi-3-scores/\">previously shown</a> those settings move ARC-AGI-3 scores substantially without changing the model. The result measures the model plus the agent system.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Other reported figures: 97.6% on <a href=\"https://epoch.ai/benchmarks/frontiermath-tier-4-v2\">FrontierMath Tier 4</a>, 95.9% on <a href=\"https://benchcad.com/news.html\">BenchCAD</a> Vision2Code against 84.3% for Fable 5.1, and 64.6% on <a href=\"https://www.tbench.ai/news/terminal-bench-science-0-1\">Terminal-Bench Science</a> against Anthropic’s reported 52.6%. Epoch AI notes OpenAI funded FrontierMath and has exclusive access to part of it.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Coding is the weak spot in the story. Astra scores 74.1% on DeepSWE v1.1 versus 70.8% for Sol. Meta reported 75.4% for Muse Spark 1.3 at maximum reasoning, and the <a href=\"https://deepswe.datacurve.ai/\">public leaderboard</a> puts Gemini 3.8 Flash and Claude Opus 5 near 74%. On a 113-task benchmark, those gaps are one or two tasks.</p>\n  <div id=\"mtp-astra-embed\">\n   <iframe class=\"lazyload\" id=\"mtp-astra-frame\" scrolling=\"no\" title=\"GPT-6 Astra interactive explainer\" srcdoc=\"&lt;style&gt;\n*{box-sizing:border-box;margin:0;padding:0}\nbody{background:#000;color:#ECECEC;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;padding:0;overflow-x:hidden}\n#astra{max-width:820px;margin:0 auto;padding:22px 18px 26px}\n.hd{border-bottom:1px solid #232323;padding-bottom:14px;margin-bottom:16px}\n.hd h2{font-size:19px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.01em;color:#fff}\n.hd p{font-size:13px;color:#8E8E8E;margin-top:5px;line-height:1.5}\n.tabs{display:flex;gap:6px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:16px}\n.tab{background:#111;border:1px solid #262626;color:#9A9A9A;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:500;padding:7px 13px;border-radius:999px;cursor:pointer;transition:all .18s;font-family:inherit}\n.tab:hover{border-color:#10A37F;color:#D6D6D6}\n.tab:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #10A37F;outline-offset:2px}\n.tab.on{background:#10A37F;border-color:#10A37F;color:#04211A}\n.panel{display:none;animation:fade .3s ease}\n.panel.on{display:block}\n@keyframes fade{from{opacity:0}to{opacity:1}}\n.stage{background:#0B0B0B;border:1px solid #1E1E1E;border-radius:10px;padding:18px}\n.stage h3{font-size:15px;font-weight:600;color:#fff;margin-bottom:6px}\n.stage p.lead{font-size:13px;color:#909090;line-height:1.6;margin-bottom:14px}\n.ctrl{background:#10A37F;color:#04211A;border:0;border-radius:6px;padding:8px 15px;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;font-family:inherit;transition:opacity .15s}\n.ctrl:hover{opacity:.85}\n.ctrl:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #fff;outline-offset:2px}\n.note{font-size:11.5px;color:#6E6E6E;line-height:1.55;margin-top:12px;border-top:1px solid #1C1C1C;padding-top:10px}\nsvg{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}\n.bars{margin-top:4px}\n.bar-row{margin-bottom:13px}\n.bar-lab{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;font-size:12px;margin-bottom:5px}\n.bar-lab span:first-child{color:#C8C8C8}\n.bar-lab span:last-child{color:#10A37F;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;font-weight:600}\n.track{height:7px;background:#1A1A1A;border-radius:4px;overflow:hidden}\n.fill{height:100%;width:0;border-radius:4px;background:#10A37F;transition:width 1.1s cubic-bezier(.16,.84,.44,1)}\n.fill.cmp{background:#3A3A3A}\n.calc{display:grid;gap:13px}\n.slider-row label{display:block;font-size:12px;color:#9A9A9A;margin-bottom:7px}\ninput[type=range]{width:100%;accent-color:#10A37F}\n.out{display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:4px}\n.cell{flex:1 1 130px;background:#101010;border:1px solid #1F1F1F;border-radius:8px;padding:11px 12px}\n.cell b{display:block;font-size:20px;color:#10A37F;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;font-weight:600}\n.cell i{display:block;font-size:11px;color:#787878;font-style:normal;margin-top:3px}\n.foot{margin-top:16px;padding-top:12px;border-top:1px solid #1C1C1C;font-size:11px;color:#5E5E5E;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap}\n.foot a{color:#10A37F;text-decoration:none}\n@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){*{animation:none!important;transition:none!important}}\n@media (max-width:640px){#astra{padding:16px 12px 20px}.hd h2{font-size:17px}.tab{font-size:11.5px;padding:6px 11px}.stage{padding:14px}.cell b{font-size:17px}}\n&lt;/style&gt;\n\n&lt;div id=&quot;astra&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;hd&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;h2&gt;GPT-6 Astra, explained in four moving parts&lt;/h2&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;Click a tab. Each panel animates the one mechanism that actually changed, using OpenAI's published numbers.&lt;/p&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n\n  &lt;div class=&quot;tabs&quot; role=&quot;tablist&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;button class=&quot;tab on&quot; data-p=&quot;0&quot; role=&quot;tab&quot;&gt;Notes vs compaction&lt;/button&gt;\n    &lt;button class=&quot;tab&quot; data-p=&quot;1&quot; role=&quot;tab&quot;&gt;The computer-use loop&lt;/button&gt;\n    &lt;button class=&quot;tab&quot; data-p=&quot;2&quot; role=&quot;tab&quot;&gt;Where it leads&lt;/button&gt;\n    &lt;button class=&quot;tab&quot; data-p=&quot;3&quot; role=&quot;tab&quot;&gt;What it costs&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n\n  &lt;div class=&quot;panel on&quot; data-p=&quot;0&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;stage&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;h3&gt;Long jobs stop getting summarized away&lt;/h3&gt;\n      &lt;p class=&quot;lead&quot;&gt;Codex used to compress old turns into a summary when context filled up. Detail about why a fix failed was lost. Astra can write notes and search back into earlier messages instead.&lt;/p&gt;\n      &lt;svg viewBox=&quot;0 0 640 200&quot; aria-label=&quot;Compaction versus notes diagram&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;text x=&quot;8&quot; y=&quot;16&quot; fill=&quot;#787878&quot; font-size=&quot;11&quot;&gt;Compaction (before)&lt;/text&gt;\n        &lt;g id=&quot;oldBlocks&quot;&gt;&lt;/g&gt;\n        &lt;path id=&quot;squash&quot; d=&quot;M 300 34 L 340 34&quot; stroke=&quot;#4A4A4A&quot; stroke-width=&quot;1.5&quot; fill=&quot;none&quot; marker-end=&quot;url(#ar)&quot;/&gt;\n        &lt;rect x=&quot;350&quot; y=&quot;24&quot; width=&quot;60&quot; height=&quot;20&quot; rx=&quot;4&quot; fill=&quot;#2A2A2A&quot;/&gt;\n        &lt;text x=&quot;380&quot; y=&quot;38&quot; fill=&quot;#8E8E8E&quot; font-size=&quot;10&quot; text-anchor=&quot;middle&quot;&gt;summary&lt;/text&gt;\n        &lt;text x=&quot;420&quot; y=&quot;38&quot; fill=&quot;#5E5E5E&quot; font-size=&quot;10&quot;&gt;detail dropped&lt;/text&gt;\n\n        &lt;text x=&quot;8&quot; y=&quot;108&quot; fill=&quot;#787878&quot; font-size=&quot;11&quot;&gt;Notes (Astra)&lt;/text&gt;\n        &lt;g id=&quot;newBlocks&quot;&gt;&lt;/g&gt;\n        &lt;path id=&quot;keep&quot; d=&quot;M 300 126 L 340 126&quot; stroke=&quot;#10A37F&quot; stroke-width=&quot;1.5&quot; fill=&quot;none&quot; marker-end=&quot;url(#arg)&quot;/&gt;\n        &lt;rect x=&quot;350&quot; y=&quot;112&quot; width=&quot;82&quot; height=&quot;28&quot; rx=&quot;4&quot; fill=&quot;#0E2A22&quot; stroke=&quot;#10A37F&quot;/&gt;\n        &lt;text x=&quot;391&quot; y=&quot;130&quot; fill=&quot;#10A37F&quot; font-size=&quot;10&quot; text-anchor=&quot;middle&quot;&gt;notes + recall&lt;/text&gt;\n        &lt;text x=&quot;442&quot; y=&quot;130&quot; fill=&quot;#5E5E5E&quot; font-size=&quot;10&quot;&gt;detail retrievable&lt;/text&gt;\n        &lt;defs&gt;\n          &lt;marker id=&quot;ar&quot; markerWidth=&quot;6&quot; markerHeight=&quot;6&quot; refX=&quot;5&quot; refY=&quot;3&quot; orient=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;path d=&quot;M0,0 L6,3 L0,6&quot; fill=&quot;#4A4A4A&quot;/&gt;&lt;/marker&gt;\n          &lt;marker id=&quot;arg&quot; markerWidth=&quot;6&quot; markerHeight=&quot;6&quot; refX=&quot;5&quot; refY=&quot;3&quot; orient=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;path d=&quot;M0,0 L6,3 L0,6&quot; fill=&quot;#10A37F&quot;/&gt;&lt;/marker&gt;\n        &lt;/defs&gt;\n      &lt;/svg&gt;\n      &lt;button class=&quot;ctrl&quot; id=&quot;replay0&quot;&gt;Fill the context window&lt;/button&gt;\n      &lt;p class=&quot;note&quot;&gt;Experimental behind a config.toml setting at launch. OpenAI says it becomes the Astra default in Codex in the coming weeks. Astra can also ask a question while continuing work that does not depend on the answer.&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n\n  &lt;div class=&quot;panel&quot; data-p=&quot;1&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;stage&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;h3&gt;It drives the screen, not an API&lt;/h3&gt;\n      &lt;p class=&quot;lead&quot;&gt;Astra reads a screenshot, decides, then clicks or types, and repeats. OpenAI demonstrated it in KiCad, Excel, Blender and Power BI, plus browser form entry and website QA.&lt;/p&gt;\n      &lt;svg viewBox=&quot;0 0 640 190&quot; aria-label=&quot;Observe plan act loop&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;circle cx=&quot;120&quot; cy=&quot;95&quot; r=&quot;42&quot; fill=&quot;none&quot; stroke=&quot;#242424&quot; stroke-width=&quot;1.5&quot;/&gt;\n        &lt;circle cx=&quot;320&quot; cy=&quot;95&quot; r=&quot;42&quot; fill=&quot;none&quot; stroke=&quot;#242424&quot; stroke-width=&quot;1.5&quot;/&gt;\n        &lt;circle cx=&quot;520&quot; cy=&quot;95&quot; r=&quot;42&quot; fill=&quot;none&quot; stroke=&quot;#242424&quot; stroke-width=&quot;1.5&quot;/&gt;\n        &lt;text x=&quot;120&quot; y=&quot;99&quot; fill=&quot;#8E8E8E&quot; font-size=&quot;12&quot; text-anchor=&quot;middle&quot;&gt;observe&lt;/text&gt;\n        &lt;text x=&quot;320&quot; y=&quot;99&quot; fill=&quot;#8E8E8E&quot; font-size=&quot;12&quot; text-anchor=&quot;middle&quot;&gt;plan&lt;/text&gt;\n        &lt;text x=&quot;520&quot; y=&quot;99&quot; fill=&quot;#8E8E8E&quot; font-size=&quot;12&quot; text-anchor=&quot;middle&quot;&gt;act&lt;/text&gt;\n        &lt;path d=&quot;M 162 95 L 278 95&quot; stroke=&quot;#242424&quot; stroke-width=&quot;1.5&quot;/&gt;\n        &lt;path d=&quot;M 362 95 L 478 95&quot; stroke=&quot;#242424&quot; stroke-width=&quot;1.5&quot;/&gt;\n        &lt;path d=&quot;M 520 137 Q 320 195 120 137&quot; stroke=&quot;#242424&quot; stroke-width=&quot;1.5&quot; fill=&quot;none&quot;/&gt;\n        &lt;circle id=&quot;dot&quot; cx=&quot;120&quot; cy=&quot;95&quot; r=&quot;6&quot; fill=&quot;#10A37F&quot;/&gt;\n        &lt;text x=&quot;320&quot; y=&quot;176&quot; fill=&quot;#5E5E5E&quot; font-size=&quot;10&quot; text-anchor=&quot;middle&quot;&gt;screen state feeds back in&lt;/text&gt;\n      &lt;/svg&gt;\n      &lt;button class=&quot;ctrl&quot; id=&quot;replay1&quot;&gt;Run one loop&lt;/button&gt;\n      &lt;p class=&quot;note&quot;&gt;On OSWorld V2-Offline, OpenAI reports 72.6% for Astra against 65.7% for GPT-5.6 Sol, and average time per task falling from about 75 minutes to 40. Anthropic reports 77.9% for Claude Fable 5.1 but says it used a different OSWorld release.&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n\n  &lt;div class=&quot;panel&quot; data-p=&quot;2&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;stage&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;h3&gt;Big gains outside coding, thinner ones inside it&lt;/h3&gt;\n      &lt;p class=&quot;lead&quot;&gt;Bars show OpenAI's reported scores. Grey is the nearest published comparison. Read the caveats below before quoting any of them.&lt;/p&gt;\n      &lt;div class=&quot;bars&quot; id=&quot;bars&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n      &lt;button class=&quot;ctrl&quot; id=&quot;replay2&quot;&gt;Animate scores&lt;/button&gt;\n      &lt;p class=&quot;note&quot;&gt;ARC-AGI-3 was run with a Responses API harness that retains reasoning across turns, so it measures the model and the agent system together. ExploitBench 100% is an aggregate capability-coverage score, not a binary pass rate. FrontierMath Tier 4 is run by Epoch AI, which OpenAI funded and has partial exclusive access to. On DeepSWE v1.1 the public leaderboard puts Gemini 3.8 Flash and Claude Opus 5 at about 74%, so Astra's 74.1% is not a clear lead.&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n\n  &lt;div class=&quot;panel&quot; data-p=&quot;3&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;stage&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;h3&gt;Price per task, not price per token&lt;/h3&gt;\n      &lt;p class=&quot;lead&quot;&gt;Astra lists at $10 per million input tokens and $50 per million output. Drag to see what a job costs, and what the same job costs on GPT-5.6 Sol at $5 and $30.&lt;/p&gt;\n      &lt;div class=&quot;calc&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;div class=&quot;slider-row&quot;&gt;\n          &lt;label&gt;Input tokens: &lt;span id=&quot;inLab&quot;&gt;200,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/label&gt;\n          &lt;input type=&quot;range&quot; id=&quot;inTok&quot; min=&quot;10000&quot; max=&quot;1000000&quot; step=&quot;10000&quot; value=&quot;200000&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;/div&gt;\n        &lt;div class=&quot;slider-row&quot;&gt;\n          &lt;label&gt;Output tokens: &lt;span id=&quot;outLab&quot;&gt;20,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/label&gt;\n          &lt;input type=&quot;range&quot; id=&quot;outTok&quot; min=&quot;1000&quot; max=&quot;128000&quot; step=&quot;1000&quot; value=&quot;20000&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;/div&gt;\n        &lt;div class=&quot;out&quot;&gt;\n          &lt;div class=&quot;cell&quot;&gt;&lt;b id=&quot;cAstra&quot;&gt;$3.00&lt;/b&gt;&lt;i&gt;Astra, one run&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n          &lt;div class=&quot;cell&quot;&gt;&lt;b id=&quot;cSol&quot;&gt;$1.60&lt;/b&gt;&lt;i&gt;Sol, one run&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n          &lt;div class=&quot;cell&quot;&gt;&lt;b id=&quot;cRatio&quot;&gt;1.9x&lt;/b&gt;&lt;i&gt;Astra vs Sol&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n        &lt;/div&gt;\n      &lt;/div&gt;\n      &lt;p class=&quot;note&quot;&gt;Cached input is $1.00 and cache writes are $12.50 per million. Requests over 272K input tokens are billed at 2x input and cache rates and 1.5x output for the whole request, which this calculator applies. Batch and Flex run at 50% of standard, Fast mode at 2x. Context window is 1,050,000 tokens with 128,000 max output.&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n\n  &lt;div class=&quot;foot&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;span&gt;Numbers from OpenAI's launch materials and model page, September 3, 2026.&lt;/span&gt;\n    &lt;span&gt;Built by &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.marktechpost.com/&quot;&gt;Marktechpost&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n\n&lt;script&gt;\n(function(){\n  var tabs=[].slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('.tab'));\n  var panels=[].slice.call(document.querySelectorAll('.panel'));\n  function sync(){var h=document.getElementById('astra').offsetHeight+40;parent.postMessage({astraHeight:h},'*');}\n  tabs.forEach(function(t){t.addEventListener('click',function(){\n    tabs.forEach(function(x){x.classList.remove('on')});\n    panels.forEach(function(x){x.classList.remove('on')});\n    t.classList.add('on');\n    var p=document.querySelector('.panel[data-p=&quot;'+t.dataset.p+'&quot;]');\n    p.classList.add('on');\n    if(t.dataset.p==='0')run0();if(t.dataset.p==='1')run1();if(t.dataset.p==='2')run2();\n    setTimeout(sync,60);\n  })});\n\n  // panel 0\n  var ob=document.getElementById('oldBlocks'),nb=document.getElementById('newBlocks');\n  function build(g,y,col){g.innerHTML='';for(var i=0;i&lt;6;i++){var r=document.createElementNS('http://www.w3.org/2000/svg','rect');\n    r.setAttribute('x',8+i*48);r.setAttribute('y',y);r.setAttribute('width',42);r.setAttribute('height',20);\n    r.setAttribute('rx',3);r.setAttribute('fill',col);r.setAttribute('opacity','0');g.appendChild(r);}}\n  function run0(){build(ob,24,'#2A2A2A');build(nb,112,'#123A2F');\n    var a=ob.children,b=nb.children;\n    for(var i=0;i&lt;6;i++){(function(i){setTimeout(function(){\n      if(a[i])a[i].setAttribute('opacity','1');\n      if(b[i])b[i].setAttribute('opacity','1');\n      if(b[i])b[i].setAttribute('stroke','#10A37F');\n    },i*150)})(i)}}\n\n  // panel 1\n  var pts=[[120,95],[320,95],[520,95],[320,168]],di=0,timer=null;\n  function run1(){var d=document.getElementById('dot');di=0;clearInterval(timer);\n    d.setAttribute('cx',120);d.setAttribute('cy',95);\n    timer=setInterval(function(){di=(di+1)%4;var p=pts[di];\n      d.style.transition='all .5s ease';d.setAttribute('cx',p[0]);d.setAttribute('cy',p[1]);\n    },700);}\n\n  // panel 2\n  var data=[\n    ['ARC-AGI-3','98.6%',98.6,'GPT-5.6 Sol 7.8%',7.8],\n    ['FrontierMath Tier 4','97.6%',97.6,'',0],\n    ['BenchCAD Vision2Code','95.9%',95.9,'Claude Fable 5.1 84.3%',84.3],\n    ['OSWorld V2-Offline','72.6%',72.6,'GPT-5.6 Sol 65.7%',65.7],\n    ['Terminal-Bench Science','64.6%',64.6,'Claude Fable 5.1 52.6%',52.6],\n    ['DeepSWE v1.1','74.1%',74.1,'GPT-5.6 Sol 70.8%',70.8],\n    ['ExploitGym','42.4%',42.4,'GPT-5.6 Sol 30.3%',30.3]\n  ];\n  var wrap=document.getElementById('bars');\n  data.forEach(function(d){\n    var h='&lt;div class=&quot;bar-row&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;bar-lab&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;'+d[0]+'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;'+d[1]+'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;'+\n    '&lt;div class=&quot;track&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;fill&quot; data-w=&quot;'+d[2]+'&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;';\n    if(d[3])h+='&lt;div class=&quot;bar-lab&quot; style=&quot;margin-top:5px&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color:#6E6E6E;font-size:11px&quot;&gt;'+d[3]+'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;'+\n    '&lt;div class=&quot;track&quot; style=&quot;height:4px&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;fill cmp&quot; data-w=&quot;'+d[4]+'&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;';\n    h+='&lt;/div&gt;';wrap.insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend',h);\n  });\n  function run2(){var f=document.querySelectorAll('#bars .fill');\n    f.forEach(function(x){x.style.width='0'});\n    setTimeout(function(){f.forEach(function(x,i){setTimeout(function(){x.style.width=x.dataset.w+'%'},i*70)})},60);}\n\n  // panel 3\n  var inT=document.getElementById('inTok'),outT=document.getElementById('outTok');\n  function fmt(n){return n.toLocaleString('en-US')}\n  function cost(i,o,pi,po){var m=i&gt;272000?1:0;var ci=(i/1e6)*pi*(m?2:1);var co=(o/1e6)*po*(m?1.5:1);return ci+co;}\n  function calc(){var i=+inT.value,o=+outT.value;\n    document.getElementById('inLab').textContent=fmt(i);\n    document.getElementById('outLab').textContent=fmt(o);\n    var a=cost(i,o,10,50),s=cost(i,o,5,30);\n    document.getElementById('cAstra').textContent='$'+a.toFixed(2);\n    document.getElementById('cSol').textContent='$'+s.toFixed(2);\n    document.getElementById('cRatio').textContent=(a/s).toFixed(1)+'x';}\n  inT.addEventListener('input',calc);outT.addEventListener('input',calc);calc();\n\n  run0();run2();\n  window.addEventListener('load',sync);setTimeout(sync,200);setTimeout(sync,900);\n})();\n&lt;/script&gt;\n\"></iframe>\n  </div>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"></p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-cyber-capability-drives-the-access-model\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Cyber capability drives the access model</strong></h2>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Astra is the first model OpenAI has designated as reaching the Critical cybersecurity threshold in its Preparedness Framework. In testing it developed exploits for hardened browsers and operating systems, and found two previously unknown V8 vulnerabilities that OpenAI says it is disclosing to maintainers.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The consequences are practical. Standard access refuses advanced cybersecurity work including exploit discovery. For API developers, a cybersecurity safety check stops a task outright rather than pausing for approval. OpenAI’s Mia Glaese warned that users outside trusted-access programs may hit slowdowns, pauses or blocks, sometimes during unrelated work.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">OpenAI reports 100% on <a href=\"https://exploitbench.ai/\">ExploitBench</a>, an aggregate capability-coverage score rather than a pass rate, and 42.4% on ExploitGym against 30.3% for Sol, with the usual six-hour time limit removed for both.</p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-pricing\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Pricing</strong></h2>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Astra costs $10 per million input tokens and $50 per million output, with cached input at $1.00. Requests above 272K input tokens bill at 2x input and 1.5x output for the full request. Batch and Flex run at 50%, Fast mode at 2x. Pro, Business and Enterprise users also get Astra Pro.</p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-key-takeaways\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Key Takeaways</strong></h2>\n  <ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n   <li>Astra is a computer-use model first: 72.6% OSWorld V2-Offline, task time down from ~75 to ~40 minutes.</li>\n   <li>Notes replace compaction in Codex, so long agent runs stop losing failure detail.</li>\n   <li>Coding gains are marginal: 74.1% DeepSWE v1.1 sits inside the leaderboard pack.</li>\n   <li>First model at OpenAI’s Critical cyber threshold; standard access refuses exploit work.</li>\n   <li>No open weights, $10/$50 per million tokens, 1.05M context, API and AWS in coming days.</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"></p>\n  <hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\">\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"></p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Check out the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://openai.com/index/gpt-6-astra/\"><strong>OpenAI announcement</strong></a>, <a href=\"https://x.com/OpenAI/status/2095595752815030713\"><strong>OpenAI on X</strong></a> and <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-6-astra\"><strong>GPT-6 Astra model page</strong></a>. Also,&nbsp;feel free to follow us on&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://x.com/intent/follow?screen_name=marktechpost\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><mark>Twitter</mark></a></strong>&nbsp;and don’t forget to join our&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/machinelearningnews/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">150k+ML SubReddit</a></strong>&nbsp;and Subscribe to&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://magic.beehiiv.com/v1/f5e63dd4-5653-4f09-83e2-321a8b1ba526?email={{email}}\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">our Newsletter</a></strong>. Wait! are you on telegram?&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://t.me/machinelearningresearchnews\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">now you can join us on telegram as well.</a></strong></p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Need to partner with us for promoting your GitHub Repo OR Hugging Face Page OR Product Release OR Webinar etc.?&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://forms.gle/wbash1wF6efRj8G58\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><mark>Connect with us</mark></a></strong></p>\n  <!-- MOLONGUI AUTHORSHIP PLUGIN 5.2.11 -->\n  <!-- https://www.molongui.com/wordpress-plugin-post-authors -->\n  <div class=\"m-a-box \" data-box-layout=\"slim\" data-box-position=\"below\" data-multiauthor=\"false\" data-author-id=\"1\" data-author-type=\"user\" data-author-archived=\"\">\n   <div class=\"m-a-box-container\">\n    <div class=\"m-a-box-tab m-a-box-content m-a-box-profile\" data-profile-layout=\"layout-1\" data-author-ref=\"user-1\" itemscope itemid=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/author/6flvq/\" itemtype=\"https://schema.org/Person\">\n     <div class=\"m-a-box-content-middle\">\n      <div class=\"m-a-box-item m-a-box-avatar\" data-source=\"local\">\n       <a class=\"m-a-box-avatar-url\" href=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/author/6flvq/\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Screen-Shot-2021-09-14-at-9.02.24-AM-150x150.png\" class=\"avatar avatar-150 photo\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Screen-Shot-2021-09-14-at-9.02.24-AM-150x150.png 150w, https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Screen-Shot-2021-09-14-at-9.02.24-AM-80x80.png 80w, https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Screen-Shot-2021-09-14-at-9.02.24-AM-24x24.png 24w, https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Screen-Shot-2021-09-14-at-9.02.24-AM-48x48.png 48w, https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Screen-Shot-2021-09-14-at-9.02.24-AM-96x96.png 96w, https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Screen-Shot-2021-09-14-at-9.02.24-AM-300x300.png 300w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px\" data-attachment-id=\"17663\" data-permalink=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/?attachment_id=17663\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Screen-Shot-2021-09-14-at-9.02.24-AM.png\" data-orig-size=\"832,778\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"Screen Shot 2021-09-14 at 9.02.24 AM\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Screen-Shot-2021-09-14-at-9.02.24-AM.png\"></a>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"m-a-box-item m-a-box-social \">\n       <div class=\"m-a-box-social-icon m-a-list-social-icon\">\n        <a class=\"m-icon-container m-ico-facebook m-ico-\" href=\"https://www.facebook.com/MarkTechPost/\" target=\"_self\" itemprop=\"sameAs\" aria-label=\"View Asif Razzaq's Facebook profile\"><i class=\"m-a-icon-facebook\"></i></a>\n       </div>\n       <div class=\"m-a-box-social-icon m-a-list-social-icon\">\n        <a class=\"m-icon-container m-ico-twitter m-ico-\" href=\"https://twitter.com/asifrazzaq1988\" target=\"_self\" itemprop=\"sameAs\" aria-label=\"View Asif Razzaq's Twitter profile\"><i class=\"m-a-icon-twitter\"></i></a>\n       </div>\n       <div class=\"m-a-box-social-icon m-a-list-social-icon\">\n        <a class=\"m-icon-container m-ico-linkedin m-ico-\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/asifrazzaq/\" target=\"_self\" itemprop=\"sameAs\" aria-label=\"View Asif Razzaq's Linkedin profile\"><i class=\"m-a-icon-linkedin\"></i></a>\n       </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"m-a-box-item m-a-box-data\">\n       <div class=\"m-a-box-name\">\n        <h5 itemprop=\"name\"><a class=\"m-a-box-name-url \" href=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/author/6flvq/\" itemprop=\"url\"> Asif Razzaq</a></h5>\n       </div>\n       <div class=\"m-a-box-item m-a-box-meta\">\n        <a href=\"https://www.marktechpost.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"m-a-box-string-web\">Website</span></a>&nbsp;<span class=\"m-a-box-meta-divider\">|</span>&nbsp; <a href=\"#\" class=\"m-a-box-data-toggle\" rel=\"nofollow\"><span class=\"m-a-box-string-more-posts\">+ posts</span></a>\n       </div>\n       <div class=\"m-a-box-bio\" itemprop=\"description\">\n        <p>Asif Razzaq is the CEO of Marktechpost Media Inc.. As a visionary entrepreneur and engineer, Asif is committed to harnessing the potential of Artificial Intelligence for social good. His most recent endeavor is the launch of an Artificial Intelligence Media Platform, Marktechpost, which stands out for its in-depth coverage of machine learning and deep learning news that is both technically sound and easily understandable by a wide audience. The platform boasts of over 2 million monthly views, illustrating its popularity among audiences.</p>\n       </div>\n       <div class=\"m-a-box-related\" data-related-layout=\"layout-1\"></div>\n      </div>\n     </div>\n    </div>\n   </div>\n  </div>\n  <!-- CONTENT END 2 -->\n </body>\n</html>",
  "aiSummary": "OpenAI 发布 GPT-6 Astra，这是一款拥有 105 万上下文窗口并设有 Critical 网络安全门槛的计算机使用模型，以上下文笔记取代压缩机制，编码能力略有提升，仅通过 API 提供，每百万 token 输入 10 美元、输出 50 美元。",
  "oneSentenceSummary": "OpenAI 发布 GPT-6 Astra，这是一款拥有 105 万上下文窗口并设有 Critical 网络安全门槛的计算机使用模型，以上下文笔记取代压缩机制，编码能力略有提升，仅通过 API 提供，每百万 token 输入 10 美元、输出 50 美元。",
  "summary": "OpenAI 已发布 GPT-6 Astra，并将其定位为计算机使用系统，而非聊天模型。其核心创新在于上下文处理：Astra 以跨上下文窗口的持久化笔记取代了 Codex 的压缩机制，从而在长时间智能体运行中保留失败细节与工具输出。该模型还可一边继续不相关的工作，一边向用户提问。模型配备 105 万 token 的上下文窗口与 12.8 万 token 的最大输出，并在 high 之上新增两个推理级别。基准测试结果：OSWorld V2-Offline 达 72.6%（任务时间从约 75 分钟降至约 40 分钟）、ARC-AGI-3 达 98.6%（已注明特定测试环境设置）、FrontierMath Tier 4 达 97.6%，DeepSWE v1.1 达 74.1%。编码被视为短板，Astra 在排行榜上与 Gemini 3.8 Flash 和 Claude Opus 5 并列，较 GPT-5.6 Sol 仅有微小差距。值得注意的是，Astra 是首个被 OpenAI 评定达到其 Critical 网络安全阈值的模型，已能针对加固系统开发漏洞利用，并发现两个此前未知的 V8 漏洞。访问需通过 Trusted Access 和 Daybreak 项目进行限制，标准 API 访问将被拒绝处理高级网络安全任务。定价为输入每百万 token 10 美元、输出每百万 token 50 美元，未发布开源权重。",
  "mainPoints": [
    {
      "point": "上下文笔记取代压缩机制，解决智能体的关键失败模式",
      "explanation": "Astra 在上下文窗口之间保持笔记，而非对早期轮次进行总结并丢弃，从而保留修复为何失败、哪些测试已运行等细节。该功能目前通过 config.toml 配置项处于实验阶段，不久将成为 Codex 的默认设置。"
    },
    {
      "point": "计算机使用与数学基准强劲，但编码提升有限",
      "explanation": "Astra 在 OSWorld V2-Offline 得分 72.6%（任务时间从约 75 分钟降至约 40 分钟），在 FrontierMath Tier 4 得分 97.6%。在编程方面，其 74.1% 的 DeepSWE v1.1 得分位于排行榜中段，与 Gemini 3.8 Flash 和 Claude Opus 5 并列，较 GPT-5.6 Sol 仅小幅领先。"
    },
    {
      "point": "首个达到 OpenAI Critical 网络安全阈值的模型，具备漏洞利用能力",
      "explanation": "Astra 针对加固的浏览器和操作系统开发了漏洞利用，并发现了两个此前未知的 V8 漏洞。标准访问权限拒绝处理高级网络安全任务；不在 Trusted Access 和 Daybreak 项目中的用户即使在不相关任务中也可能遇到减速、暂停或拦截。"
    },
    {
      "point": "仅 API 可用，每百万 token 定价 10 美元 / 50 美元，无开源权重",
      "explanation": "Astra 为闭源托管模型，输入支持文本和图片，输出为文本，不支持微调。定价含缓存输入每百万 1.00 美元，超过 272K token 的请求另有附加费。"
    }
  ],
  "keyQuotes": [
    "编码是整个故事中的短板。",
    "Astra 是 OpenAI 在 Preparedness Framework 中首个被认定为达到 Critical 网络安全阈值的模型。",
    "对开发者而言最主要的变化是上下文处理。Codex 此前使用压缩机制，在上下文填满后对早期轮次进行总结，而该过程会丢弃智能体后续所需的细节。"
  ],
